{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"heavensent-nonproift-galago","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nCloud and DC need one provider-neutral definition of logical identity, attempts, delay, ambiguity, and terminal outcome before either adapter can remove nested retries.\n\n## Outcome\nAdd immutable operation/outcome values and the sole three-invocation, 15-second cumulative-sleep budget. Establish ADR 0100 as a provisional S1 decision record; adapter and dispatch wiring remain later tasks.\n\n## Plan\n1. Define typed values for logical id, desired postcondition, invocation/request counts, disposition, failure scope, replay safety, delay source/value, `retry_not_before`, and bounded redacted diagnostics.\n2. Implement a fake-clock budget with at most three physical invocations and 15 seconds cumulative sleep. Use `2**(attempt+1)+U[0,1)`: [2s,3s), then [4s,5s).\n3. Treat authoritative provider delay as a lower bound. If it cannot fit, return `retry_not_before` without sleep or fictional attempt.\n4. Define ambiguity decisions: observed desired state is recovered success; conclusive old state may replay; failed/inconclusive observation is non-replaying `commit_unknown`.\n5. Seed ADR 0100 with retry ownership, Jira no-idempotency constraint, observe-before-replay, lifecycle owners, and selected-route-only deltas.\n\n## Testing\nUse deterministic UUID/jitter/fake-clock tables. Assert every field, deadline, count, and diagnostic bound.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Outcome objects expose all named provider-neutral fields with deterministic serialization.\n- [ ] One logical id remains stable across every physical invocation.\n- [ ] No budget permits more than three invocations or 15 seconds cumulative sleep.\n- [ ] Fallback delays remain [2s,3s) then [4s,5s).\n- [ ] Over-budget authoritative delay returns `retry_not_before` without sleeping or incrementing an attempt.\n- [ ] Ambiguity decisions distinguish recovered success, safe replay, and non-replaying `commit_unknown`.\n- [ ] ADR 0100 records the provisional contract and ownership boundaries.\n\n## Out of scope\nCloud/DC execution and legacy dispatch integration are later S1 tasks.","id":"7bc2-5203-d5f4-4a4a","parent_id":"f5ac-6373-5e33-4374","priority":1,"tags":["rp03","retry","tdd","adr"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S1 T1 — Define the logical-operation outcome and retry budget"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787027803458158001,"uuid":"1c765840-bb52-48bd-97ea-44584a23f88a"}